WEBVTT

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:28.745
Oh, I fear I may not survive this war reenactment.

00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:31.914
I can't believe we're only
12 feet from the parking lot.

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:35.543
This is every bit as fun as the real Civil War.

00:00:35.627 --> 00:00:39.714
Not the Civil War, Private.
We're reenacting the Sith-il War.

00:00:39.798 --> 00:00:41.799
Sith? What the Hoth?

00:00:41.884 --> 00:00:44.635
Enemy invaders!
Up in yonder sky!

00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:01.536
I am Darth Stroyer.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.331
Darth Stroyer? That's the
stupidest name I've ever heard.

00:01:05.415 --> 00:01:06.541
Let's hear the rest.

00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:08.835
Darth Trocious.

00:01:09.461 --> 00:01:10.753
Darth Sploder.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.964
Darth Urderer.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:15.424
Darth It-head.

00:01:18.595 --> 00:01:20.304
Company, attack!

00:01:25.269 --> 00:01:28.062
Don't fire until you see
the greens of their eyes!

00:01:28.397 --> 00:01:29.689
It saves on bullets.

00:01:44.872 --> 00:01:47.874
I shall rip out your heart
and show it to you.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:50.877
It is done.

00:01:51.003 --> 00:01:54.714
The candle that burns twice
as bright burns half as long.

00:02:00.429 --> 00:02:01.846
You're dead.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.348
No, I'm just very old.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.271
Whoa. That's good acting.

00:02:10.355 --> 00:02:12.398
It's payback time,
Sploder.

00:02:18.322 --> 00:02:23.075
Tell my mother to pick me up
outside Quiznos.

00:02:24.786 --> 00:02:26.245
That's three dead.

00:02:26.872 --> 00:02:28.414
Let's pick up the pace,
people.

00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:29.916
At this point in
the actual war,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.376
the death toll
was 98 million.

00:02:32.836 --> 00:02:36.005
You humans
and your fragile organs.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.674
One little stab
to the goo, and...

00:02:40.177 --> 00:02:42.053
You're dead, Earth man.

00:02:42.971 --> 00:02:45.014
Cruel fate, I'm dead.

00:02:45.223 --> 00:02:47.183
They're putting me
in my Sunday suit

00:02:47.309 --> 00:02:49.226
and shoving me
in a wooden box.

00:02:50.187 --> 00:02:54.190
Now they're lowering me
into the cold, cold ground.

00:02:54.483 --> 00:02:57.485
Hello,
here come the worms.

00:02:58.445 --> 00:03:01.072
If you were really dead, you
wouldn't be laughing so hard.

00:03:02.366 --> 00:03:05.159
Yeah, death's a big deal
to you flesh bags.

00:03:05.243 --> 00:03:08.245
But in case you didn't notice, I'm a robot.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.332
So? What if something heavy
fell on you, like a church?

00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:12.500
You could still die.

00:03:12.584 --> 00:03:13.793
Nuh-uh!

00:03:13.877 --> 00:03:17.088
My wireless backup unit
saves a copy of me every day.

00:03:17.172 --> 00:03:19.674
So, if my body gets killed,
big whoop,

00:03:19.758 --> 00:03:21.926
I just download
into another body.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.302
I'm immortal, baby.

00:03:23.387 --> 00:03:25.304
What? Then how come
you always scream

00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:27.014
so much when
you're in danger?

00:03:27.224 --> 00:03:29.767
I never said I wasn't
a drama queen.

00:03:30.435 --> 00:03:33.104
And the winner
of the war is...

00:03:34.106 --> 00:03:36.107
Let me just cross-check
my tabulation here.

00:03:36.566 --> 00:03:38.484
Factor in the corsages
for the widows...

00:03:38.568 --> 00:03:41.362
Hurry up, you number-crunching
crumb-nuncher!

00:03:41.446 --> 00:03:43.823
Everybody but me
is dying of old age!

00:03:43.949 --> 00:03:45.241
Okay.

00:03:45.909 --> 00:03:50.705
The winners, at a net cost of only
$12 per life cut tragically short,

00:03:50.789 --> 00:03:52.748
our Sith Overlords!

00:03:52.916 --> 00:03:54.125
Yeah!
Yes!

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:56.669
Hot diggity. I mean,

00:03:56.753 --> 00:03:59.755
supreme diggity.

00:04:00.757 --> 00:04:05.302
Good war,
good war, good war...

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.438
It may have been a fake war, but
my scuffed knee is all too real.

00:04:15.522 --> 00:04:19.191
I've got pains in joints
I had removed a century ago.

00:04:19.276 --> 00:04:22.862
Bender, bring me my soft
chair with the wheels on it.

00:04:22.946 --> 00:04:25.448
Your wheelchair?
I don't need a wheelchair!

00:04:25.532 --> 00:04:27.366
The one with the wheels!

00:04:27.451 --> 00:04:29.535
Poor flimsy humans.

00:04:29.619 --> 00:04:32.121
Don't you wish you were
flawless like me?

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:34.749
A towering inferno of
physical perfection?

00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:38.419
I hate to pop your blimp-like
ego, but you are not perfect.

00:04:38.503 --> 00:04:40.046
Am so.
Are not.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.756
Is too!
Says who?

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.801
Says the only human whose
opinion I even remotely respect.

00:04:48.555 --> 00:04:52.558
Inspector 5, the best inspector a kid could want.

00:04:52.726 --> 00:04:54.977
The day I was built,
he looked me over,

00:04:55.145 --> 00:04:57.396
probably with tears
of pride in his eyes,

00:04:57.481 --> 00:04:59.440
and proclaimed
to all the world,

00:04:59.566 --> 00:05:01.567
by means of this
scrap of paper,

00:05:01.651 --> 00:05:05.529
that I was perfect and
infallible in every way.

00:05:06.114 --> 00:05:07.531
Hey, Mr. Perfect,

00:05:07.616 --> 00:05:09.283
you wet the chair.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:13.996
Huh? It wasn't me. Must be some of
that urine you're all so proud of.

00:05:15.582 --> 00:05:17.458
That's not urine.
It's oil.

00:05:17.542 --> 00:05:20.795
Impossible. I'm triple-sealed
to prevent any chance of...

00:05:23.507 --> 00:05:25.216
You call that
an ink defense?

00:05:28.512 --> 00:05:30.054
Goodbye, friends.

00:05:32.307 --> 00:05:33.724
What could have
caused the leak?

00:05:33.809 --> 00:05:36.018
Excessive heat, on account of I'm so hot?

00:05:36.686 --> 00:05:37.978
Alas, no.

00:05:38.063 --> 00:05:42.441
Oh, Bender, I'm afraid it's
a symptom of a fatal defect.

00:05:42.526 --> 00:05:44.026
Yeah, fatal, schmatal.

00:05:44.111 --> 00:05:46.862
If I die, I can just
download my backup copy

00:05:46.947 --> 00:05:49.406
into a new,
equally fabulous body.

00:05:49.491 --> 00:05:54.537
That's just it. You can't! You
were built without a backup unit!

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:57.790
There's no backup
copy of me?

00:05:57.874 --> 00:06:00.501
That's what I just said,
you mortal coil.

00:06:00.752 --> 00:06:02.253
So, if I die...

00:06:02.337 --> 00:06:04.880
You die.
Or as you put it...

00:06:06.716 --> 00:06:08.634
Excuse me for a moment.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.809
No!

00:06:22.774 --> 00:06:25.192
I can't believe it!
I'm gonna die!

00:06:25.277 --> 00:06:27.611
How much time does he have left, Professor?

00:06:27.696 --> 00:06:30.239
Between a minute
and a billion years.

00:06:30.448 --> 00:06:32.533
Well, at least you
can plan accordingly.

00:06:32.617 --> 00:06:34.118
Dying sucks butt!

00:06:34.202 --> 00:06:36.537
How do you living beings
cope with mortality?

00:06:36.621 --> 00:06:37.872
Violent outbursts.

00:06:37.998 --> 00:06:39.248
General sluttiness.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.417
Thanks to denial,
I'm immortal.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.586
Damn it, I'm supposed to be perfect!

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:46.213
Inspector 5 gave me
his blessing!

00:06:46.298 --> 00:06:48.924
How could he bring me into
this world knowing I would die?

00:06:49.009 --> 00:06:51.302
So you wish you
were never born, maybe?

00:06:51.386 --> 00:06:55.514
Yes, anything less than immortality
is a complete waste of time!

00:06:55.599 --> 00:06:57.183
Then suicide it is.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:07:00.644
Step into my office. I'll
give you a nice Kevorking.

00:07:00.729 --> 00:07:04.899
Not until I hunt down Inspector 5
and beat an explanation out of him!

00:07:04.983 --> 00:07:07.735
I'm all for a good beating,
but you'll never find him.

00:07:07.819 --> 00:07:09.820
Product inspectors
are bureaucrats,

00:07:09.905 --> 00:07:12.656
faceless bean-counters
who blend into the woodwork.

00:07:12.908 --> 00:07:14.325
I beg to differ.

00:07:14.492 --> 00:07:16.619
Stinking bureaucrats.
I hate them!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.039
Then again, you might be able to find Inspector 5

00:07:20.123 --> 00:07:22.291
with the help of another
seasoned bureaucrat.

00:07:22.626 --> 00:07:24.210
Hermes, old pal.

00:07:24.294 --> 00:07:28.005
Old pal? 8.5 seconds ago,
you said you hated me.

00:07:28.089 --> 00:07:30.049
Time heals all wounds.

00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:32.259
You know what?
I will help you,

00:07:32.344 --> 00:07:35.429
but only to prove I'm not just
a paper-pushing file jockey.

00:07:35.513 --> 00:07:37.723
Will you be taking your
portable filing cabinet?

00:07:37.849 --> 00:07:39.141
None of your beeswax.

00:07:41.311 --> 00:07:43.729
I'll only be away an hour,
but I'm counting on you

00:07:43.813 --> 00:07:46.148
to do the all-critical
filing in my absence.

00:07:46.233 --> 00:07:48.567
Shall we review
alphabetical order?

00:07:48.652 --> 00:07:50.027
A, B, C, D...

00:07:50.111 --> 00:07:51.445
Get out of my office!

00:07:55.992 --> 00:07:59.036
Yes, I'd like to request
a death certificate.

00:08:00.538 --> 00:08:02.539
Sorry,
that's Building C.

00:08:02.832 --> 00:08:06.001
The Central Bureaucracy maintains
records on all bureaucrats.

00:08:06.127 --> 00:08:08.254
We should be able to
look up Inspector 5.

00:08:12.842 --> 00:08:14.927
Application for
ingress approved.

00:08:15.178 --> 00:08:16.971
And the other
potential entrant?

00:08:17.681 --> 00:08:18.931
He's my pencil sharpener.

00:08:19.057 --> 00:08:20.349
You betcha!

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.271
Proceed.

00:08:40.161 --> 00:08:42.955
I maintain a cubicle here
for weekend getaways.

00:08:48.044 --> 00:08:51.088
Wow. Until now, I thought
giant cubes were exciting.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.897
I did like the part
where they screamed.

00:09:11.276 --> 00:09:13.986
This is mine, right next to the center square.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:18.282
Sorry, Hermes,
I drank all your Wite-Out.

00:09:19.284 --> 00:09:22.619
Once I log in, I can access
Inspector 5's profile.

00:09:26.916 --> 00:09:28.500
Damn it, it won't go on!

00:09:28.585 --> 00:09:30.085
That's because
you're not me.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.087
Hooray, it won't go on!

00:09:32.172 --> 00:09:33.964
The bureaucra-scan
won't let anyone

00:09:34.049 --> 00:09:35.799
but the assigned
bureaucrat log in.

00:09:39.763 --> 00:09:42.890
Also, you have a rectangular mass in your colon.

00:09:42.974 --> 00:09:45.768
That's a calculator.
I ate it to gain its power.

00:09:45.852 --> 00:09:49.855
You locate Inspector 5 while I
slip into my ass-kicking feet.

00:09:51.232 --> 00:09:54.193
Sweet file-not-found
of Puget Sound.

00:09:54.277 --> 00:09:55.986
His record's been blanked.

00:09:56.112 --> 00:09:57.237
Oh, man!

00:09:57.322 --> 00:10:00.949
How am I gonna find some anonymous
guy I don't know anything about?

00:10:01.034 --> 00:10:04.870
I recommend the men's room
at the TWA Terminal.

00:10:14.964 --> 00:10:17.508
Okay, just file it
alphabetically.

00:10:17.592 --> 00:10:19.593
A, B, C, D...

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.180
Well, this requires
a little extra thought.

00:10:26.309 --> 00:10:27.810
I'm a natural.

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:31.855
The information we need will
be here, in the physical files.

00:10:32.148 --> 00:10:35.442
Those bastards won't know
what leafed through them.

00:10:46.162 --> 00:10:47.371
It's on.

00:10:51.626 --> 00:10:53.585
No! This is impossible!

00:10:53.795 --> 00:10:55.504
Quit blacking out
and look at this.

00:10:55.713 --> 00:10:59.675
"Inspector 1, 2, 3, 4, 6".

00:11:00.009 --> 00:11:02.344
There's no trace
of Inspector 5!

00:11:02.429 --> 00:11:04.138
But 5's the one we want!

00:11:04.222 --> 00:11:08.267
Maybe if I kicked the asses of
Inspector 2, plus Inspector 3...

00:11:08.351 --> 00:11:10.561
Addition never
solved anything, man.

00:11:10.645 --> 00:11:13.021
Let's cut our losses
and go home.

00:11:16.192 --> 00:11:17.943
So I'm doomed to die,

00:11:18.027 --> 00:11:21.029
and I'll never even get to
punch whoever's responsible?

00:11:21.781 --> 00:11:23.115
What's the point?

00:11:23.324 --> 00:11:26.785
Bender, no! Suicide isn't
necessarily the answer.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:30.372
It's not a suicide booth, you
lard-ass. It's a phone booth.

00:11:31.332 --> 00:11:33.125
They have phones
in booths now?

00:11:33.209 --> 00:11:36.044
Finally, I don't have to
lug this cell phone around.

00:11:42.469 --> 00:11:45.179
Who the hell is this?
How did you get this number?

00:11:45.263 --> 00:11:46.763
Is this the robot company?

00:11:46.848 --> 00:11:49.475
'Cause I have a complaint
about a defective robot.

00:11:49.559 --> 00:11:50.934
His name is me!

00:11:51.102 --> 00:11:53.520
A defective robot, you say?

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.107
Stay right there, dearie.

00:11:57.192 --> 00:11:59.902
I'll have tech support
take care of you.

00:12:01.738 --> 00:12:03.655
Well, things are
starting to look up.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.823
Look up!

00:12:10.413 --> 00:12:12.331
Who did you call?
Dial-a-bomb?

00:12:12.415 --> 00:12:15.709
No, I just told the robot company I was defective.

00:12:15.835 --> 00:12:17.961
You dumb cocktail shaker!

00:12:18.046 --> 00:12:21.006
Mom won't allow a defective
product to tarnish her good name!

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:22.132
She'll kill you!

00:12:22.217 --> 00:12:24.843
Big whoop. I'll just
download into a new...

00:12:24.928 --> 00:12:27.638
Oh, right.
If I die, I die.

00:12:27.847 --> 00:12:29.223
Speaking of which...

00:12:29.307 --> 00:12:32.100
You're right. You're right. You're right.

00:12:33.269 --> 00:12:36.188
That's what you get
for calling tech support.

00:12:46.366 --> 00:12:49.076
I can't run anymore.
I'll have to skip.

00:12:57.293 --> 00:12:58.377
Just a few more feet.

00:12:58.461 --> 00:13:01.463
We have to get to that pile of dead bears by 7:38.

00:13:01.548 --> 00:13:05.300
A pile of dead bears can only
mean one thing. But what?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.639
It's the 7:38!

00:13:11.057 --> 00:13:12.182
Jump!

00:13:15.144 --> 00:13:17.145
Shoot!
Someone said shoot.

00:13:36.165 --> 00:13:37.499
Well, we're boned.

00:13:37.584 --> 00:13:38.667
No, we're not!

00:13:38.751 --> 00:13:40.085
We just got to limbo.

00:13:40.169 --> 00:13:43.964
But I'm not designed to bend
that low, not without limbo music.

00:13:46.134 --> 00:13:47.634
That'll do it!

00:13:47.844 --> 00:13:49.469
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:13:51.556 --> 00:13:52.764
We're gonna get fired.

00:13:52.849 --> 00:13:54.016
Someone said fire.

00:14:05.486 --> 00:14:06.612
We did it!

00:14:06.696 --> 00:14:08.447
Twelve straight hours
of limbo.

00:14:08.531 --> 00:14:10.324
I haven't done that
since my honeymoon.

00:14:10.408 --> 00:14:12.784
Hermes, Hermes, remember that flock of bats?

00:14:12.869 --> 00:14:13.952
I sure do.

00:14:14.037 --> 00:14:15.203
That was fun.

00:14:16.205 --> 00:14:17.414
Where are we?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.915
I have no idea.

00:14:27.383 --> 00:14:30.844
Hey, we're just a stone's throw from Tijuana.

00:14:30.928 --> 00:14:32.012
See?

00:14:34.974 --> 00:14:39.770
A rock has fallen here,
in the outskirts of Tijuana.

00:14:40.063 --> 00:14:41.688
Is it within
the city limit?

00:14:41.773 --> 00:14:43.357
I think, yes.

00:14:43.441 --> 00:14:44.483
Told you.

00:14:44.567 --> 00:14:46.443
Hey, you want to
celebrate our escape?

00:14:46.527 --> 00:14:49.446
Maybe grab a shot of tequila and
take in a big-league cockfight?

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.324
Sure. No, wait.
I was built in Tijuana.

00:14:52.408 --> 00:14:54.993
Maybe Inspector 5
still works there.

00:14:55.078 --> 00:15:00.040
He better do some explaining before
I mash up some face guacamole.

00:15:02.752 --> 00:15:05.754
He's Mexican, I'm Mexican.
Let me handle this.

00:15:09.759 --> 00:15:10.967
Si!

00:15:11.469 --> 00:15:12.678
Ouch-o!

00:15:14.931 --> 00:15:16.682
Here are our passports,
visas,

00:15:16.766 --> 00:15:18.475
and Homeland Security
permission slips,

00:15:18.559 --> 00:15:20.310
notarized and starched.

00:15:22.271 --> 00:15:25.065
Okay. I also would
have accepted a bribe.

00:15:26.609 --> 00:15:28.360
Nice work, butterball.

00:15:28.486 --> 00:15:31.655
You know,
I was in Italy last week.

00:15:35.785 --> 00:15:38.120
My birthplace.
It's closed!

00:15:38.287 --> 00:15:39.788
There's not even
a shrine to me.

00:15:39.872 --> 00:15:42.708
With a gift shop,
selling piсatas of me!

00:15:42.792 --> 00:15:44.126
End of the line, man.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.212
Come on, we can still catch
a twi-night double cockfight.

00:15:47.296 --> 00:15:50.132
No, wait! What's that
in the Mexican garbage?

00:15:50.216 --> 00:15:52.259
Looks like
a half-eaten cheese diaper.

00:15:52.343 --> 00:15:53.468
No, next to that.

00:15:55.638 --> 00:15:57.973
A half-eaten
employee directory.

00:15:59.642 --> 00:16:01.560
Inspector 5's home address!

00:16:01.644 --> 00:16:04.312
His ass-ias is gracias!

00:16:15.742 --> 00:16:17.451
Where are you hiding,
you coward?

00:16:17.535 --> 00:16:19.703
Get out here and get
murdered like a man!

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:24.666
Bender, I'm afraid our search is
at an end. He's obviously long gone.

00:16:24.751 --> 00:16:26.084
Oh, yeah?

00:16:26.169 --> 00:16:28.670
Well, maybe this is
him in a costume!

00:16:29.338 --> 00:16:32.591
I'm gonna squeeze you out of
there like Tijuana toothpaste!

00:16:39.098 --> 00:16:41.600
Okay, Bender,
you're mortal.

00:16:41.684 --> 00:16:44.227
And, okay,
Inspector 5 screwed up.

00:16:44.312 --> 00:16:47.522
But that just makes the time you
have left all the more precious.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.818
Do you really want to waste the rest of
your life in a bitter, homicidal rage?

00:16:51.903 --> 00:16:54.446
No! Yes!

00:16:55.406 --> 00:16:57.532
I don't know!

00:17:05.166 --> 00:17:08.210
Why?
Why did he do this to me?

00:17:08.586 --> 00:17:11.546
All I wanted was
a little quality control.

00:17:11.714 --> 00:17:14.883
But he didn't care enough.
And now I'm gonna die!

00:17:15.426 --> 00:17:18.804
I deserve better!
I'm Bender, damn it!

00:17:18.888 --> 00:17:21.014
I'm Bender!

00:17:23.226 --> 00:17:26.102
There, there, man.
It's gonna be okay.

00:17:26.187 --> 00:17:30.357
You are Bender, which is something
Inspector 5 will never be.

00:17:31.734 --> 00:17:34.110
You know what?
You're right.

00:17:34.195 --> 00:17:36.154
He was just
a stupid bureaucrat.

00:17:36.239 --> 00:17:38.448
A stupid,
paper-pushing bureaucrat.

00:17:38.533 --> 00:17:41.159
A stupid I-dotting,
chair-squashing...

00:17:41.244 --> 00:17:42.536
Oh.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.121
No offense, Hermes.
You're not like that.

00:17:45.206 --> 00:17:47.999
I mean, you're exactly
like that, but you're okay!

00:17:48.084 --> 00:17:51.837
In fact, I'm putting you
on the do-not-kill list.

00:17:53.172 --> 00:17:55.966
Come on, fellow mortal.
We're in Tijuana.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.592
I want to live a little.

00:17:58.261 --> 00:18:01.471
Help! I'm gonna die! That's
the opposite of what I want!

00:18:06.978 --> 00:18:08.478
Quick, run out the back!

00:18:08.563 --> 00:18:11.356
I'll hack into Inspector 5's
terminal and fake your death,

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.816
so they'll call
off the kill-bots.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.818
You know that
terminal is unhackable!

00:18:14.944 --> 00:18:17.028
I'm not leaving you,
and that's final!

00:18:17.613 --> 00:18:18.738
Good luck, buddy.

00:18:29.959 --> 00:18:31.668
Bender terminated.

00:18:31.752 --> 00:18:33.044
Bender saved.

00:18:35.298 --> 00:18:38.008
Cease fire.
Mom called off the attack.

00:18:38.092 --> 00:18:40.635
Although I don't see how it's
her. Someone said, "Howitzer!"

00:18:43.306 --> 00:18:44.681
Yeah!

00:18:44.765 --> 00:18:46.641
All right! Yeah!

00:18:59.864 --> 00:19:00.989
He did it!

00:19:01.616 --> 00:19:04.367
And he's not looking back
at that cool explosion.

00:19:04.577 --> 00:19:06.328
He's a hero!

00:19:10.374 --> 00:19:12.250
What's happening?

00:19:12.335 --> 00:19:15.337
The phone's been disconnected,
the ship's repossessed,

00:19:15.421 --> 00:19:17.088
and Zoidberg's
getting overcooked!

00:19:20.551 --> 00:19:22.344
This place never changes.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.971
Leela, what in the name
of Jah happened?

00:19:25.139 --> 00:19:28.600
Too much papers!
Not enough hiding plants!

00:19:28.684 --> 00:19:29.768
It's all right.

00:19:29.852 --> 00:19:32.646
This place just needs
a one-hour bureaucratizing.

00:19:37.443 --> 00:19:39.110
You make it
look so easy.

00:19:39.195 --> 00:19:41.821
I've smoked a lot
of paperwork in my day.

00:19:41.906 --> 00:19:43.281
Hey, Bender,
did you ever find

00:19:43.366 --> 00:19:45.158
that inspector guy
you were looking for?

00:19:45.242 --> 00:19:47.494
Nah, but thanks
to this knucklehead,

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.871
I did find a new
outlook on life.

00:19:50.039 --> 00:19:51.456
It's precious and sacred.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.501
And you only get so many
millions of years on this Earth.

00:19:54.585 --> 00:19:56.211
So, let's get brick-faced!

